# SwiftFormat (https://github.com/nicklockwood/SwiftFormat) — run `swiftformat .`
# locally; CI runs `swiftformat . --lint`. Defaults, minus the pure-churn rules
# below. SwiftLint owns style *checks*; SwiftFormat owns layout.
--swiftversion 6.2
--maxwidth 120
--indent 4
--decimalgrouping ignore

# Disabled on purpose:
#   wrap*Bodies / wrapLoopBodies — this codebase leans on one-line guards
#     (`guard x else { return }`, `if a { b() }`); forcing them multi-line is noise.
#   swiftTestingTestCaseNames — renames every @Test function; no value here.
#   docComments — flips `//` <-> `///` heuristically and gets it wrong on notes
#     that sit above declarations but aren't API docs.
--disable wrapIfStatementBodies,wrapPropertyBodies,wrapFunctionBodies,wrapLoopBodies
--disable swiftTestingTestCaseNames,docComments
#   redundantSelf — stripped a `self.` that Swift 6 capture semantics require
#     (AutoResumeCoordinator) and broke the build; not worth the risk.
--disable redundantSelf
#   wrapMultilineStatementBraces — SwiftLint's opening_brace rejects `{` on its
#     own line after a multi-line `if`/`guard`; SwiftLint wins on this one.
--disable wrapMultilineStatementBraces

--exclude .build,dist,DerivedData,ClaudeMeter.xcodeproj
